# Implementations README

This directory contains the implementation code for the Rhyme signature algorithm.

## Directory Structure

```
Implementations/
├── Reference_Implementation/
│   ├── Rhyme-128/
│   ├── Rhyme-256/
│   ├── Rhyme-384/
│   └── Rhyme-512/
├── Optimized_Implementation/
│   ├── Rhyme-128/
│   ├── Rhyme-256/
│   ├── Rhyme-384/
│   └── Rhyme-512/
├── Additional_Implementation/
│   └── README
└── README
```

## Directory Description

`Reference_Implementation/` contains the reference (portable) implementation of Rhyme.
Built with `-DRHYME_NO_AES`, it uses pure SHAKE-based symmetric primitives and
has no platform-specific instruction requirements.

`Optimized_Implementation/` contains the optimized implementation for mainstream
64-bit PC platforms (x86-64 with AES-NI and SSSE3).  It uses AES-256-CTR via
AES-NI intrinsics for all expansion and sampling streams, which provides
substantially faster signing.

`Additional_Implementation/` is reserved for additional platform-specific
implementations. No additional implementation is included.

## Common File Description

`api.h`: public API parameters and byte lengths (includes params.h and sign.h).

`SIG_AlgorithmInstance.c/h`: API_PKC-compatible wrapper for key generation, signing,
and verification. These translate between the API_PKC `sig_*` interface and
Rhyme's native `crypto_sign_*` functions.

`KAT_SIG.c`: known-answer test driver for the signature algorithm.  Generates
10 deterministic KAT vectors using the SM3-based DRNG.

`drng.c/h`: SM3-based deterministic random number generator used by the KAT driver
and to seed key generation.

`randombytes.c`: DRNG-backed replacement for the system `/dev/urandom` randombytes,
ensuring deterministic KAT output.

`auxfunc.c/h`: auxiliary functions from the API_PKC template.

`include/`: public headers and parameter definitions (params.h, config.h, sign.h,
symmetric.h, etc.).

`src/`: core Rhyme implementation source files.

`Makefile`: build script for the instance.

## Instances

Rhyme has four parameter sets (security levels), selected via `-DRHYME_MODE`:

| Instance    | Mode | N    | Q     | K | L | Security (bits) |
|-------------|------|------|-------|---|---|-----------------|
| Rhyme-128   | 128  | 256  | 3329  | 2 | 3 | 128             |
| Rhyme-256   | 256  | 512  | 9473  | 2 | 3 | 256             |
| Rhyme-384   | 384  | 512  | 11777 | 3 | 4 | 384             |
| Rhyme-512   | 512  | 1024 | 18433 | 2 | 3 | 512             |

## Build and Run

Run the reference KAT:

```bash
cd Reference_Implementation/Rhyme-128
make clean
make
./KAT_SIG
```

Run the optimized KAT:

```bash
cd Optimized_Implementation/Rhyme-128
make clean
make
./KAT_SIG
```

The Optimized build requires AES-NI and SSSE3 support (`-maes -mssse3`).
The Reference build has no platform-specific requirements.
